{
  "requirement": "When `habeas author` assesses a subject with existing evidence, that evidence\nMUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment. Its inputs,\ndetermination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` or otherwise be\nsupplied to the model. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs\nsupplied to it, so sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer\nexist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. Each obligation maps to marked code and a marked test, with one judgment call noted at the end.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. Existing evidence MUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment.\n2. Its inputs MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set.\n3. Its determination MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set.\n4. Its rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set.\n5. Its inputs, determination, and rationale MUST NOT otherwise be supplied to the model.\n6. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs supplied to it, so unresolvable or irrelevant earlier sources cannot block or shape reassessment.\n\n**Code**\n- **Obligation 1:** `select_subjects` and `current` in `src/authoring/batch.rs`, called from `run_batch` (reached via `author_all_with_options`, which carries the `{impl}`). They use the loaded evidence state (Valid, Fixme, or DeterminationFalse) only to decide whether a subject is skipped as unchanged or queued. The evidence content is never passed on to the assessment.\n- **Obligations 2–4:** `AssessmentSources::prepare` in `src/authoring/inputs.rs` builds the mandatory set only from the following. It never reads `evidence/<subject>.json`.\n  - The subject's declaration.\n  - Its `{cite}` targets.\n  - Its current `{impl}`, `{test}`, and `{fixme}` edges.\n  - Its anchors.\n  - Definition dependencies and built-ins.\n- **Generated evidence omission:** `generated_evidence_selector`, `generated_evidence_path`, `SourceAccess::omit_generated_evidence`, and `source_input` omit selectors and references located under `evidence/`, including symlink aliases.\n- **Obligation 5:** `initial_prompt` builds the prompt only from `model_mandatory_inputs()`, which clones `self.mandatory`. `converse` seeds `pending` from `mandatory_inputs()`. The model's tools exclude generated `evidence/`.\n- **Obligation 6:** `AssessmentSources.recorded` starts as `Vec::new()`. It is filled only by `record_inputs`, which `converse` calls with the inputs actually delivered after a successful response. `record()` writes `recorded_inputs()`. Earlier-evidence inputs are never in `recorded`, so missing or removed earlier sources cannot block or shape reassessment.\n\n**Tests, all carrying `{test}` references to this requirement**\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` writes old evidence with a `notes.txt` input and an \"old secret judgment\" rationale. It asserts the mandatory inputs contain neither, and that `recorded_inputs()` is empty after `prepare`.\n- `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` plants earlier inputs whose files, items, and requirements no longer exist. It asserts `prepare` still succeeds and the mandatory set contains only the subject.\n- `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` asserts the supplied inputs omit `notes.txt`, `evidence/`, and the old rationale, and that the old file is left unchanged.\n\n**Judgment call:** the tools-level exclusion of `evidence/` from model reads is tested in `src/authoring/tools.rs` under `generated_evidence_is_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery`, which has no `{test}` reference to this requirement. That behavior belongs to `requirements.authoring.source_tools` and `requirements.configuration.evidence_paths`, not to this requirement's own obligations, so I did not count the missing reference as a gap.",
  "references": "50148c9cfa29314fa2a17847f5b31dd0d0dbff0707c70e2e20cb993a124bd5c8",
